    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_88e564376427c4c083b3543e232731303711475349afe748e4583b1e2f485cd1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The asymptotic analysis is staged as spectral localization before saddle extraction: uniform contour estimates make the holomorphic contribution and far, small, and positive real-spectral ranges negligible under the smoothing hypotheses; the remaining negative Maass window admits a saddle analysis first in the inner variable and then in the outer integral, and a cited spectral mean-value bound controls the summed approximation error.",
